<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
<h1>50cc Motorbike Hanoi: Students Passenger Use</h1>
<p>Students in Hanoi ride together constantly. A classmate needs a lift to campus, a friend is heading the same way after class, and the empty seat behind you turns a solo errand into a shared one. On a rented 50cc this is normal life, but it is also the situation where the smallest machines work hardest, and where the rider behind the bars carries responsibility for two people. This page is a straight answer to the question every student renter eventually asks: what actually changes when a passenger climbs on, and how do you do it well. The rental counter at 112 Nguyen Van Cu, Long Bien, Hanoi, open daily from 09:00 to 21:00, rents 50cc scooters and motorbikes at 200,000 VND per day.</p>
<p>This guide belongs to the <a href="/hanoi-50cc-motorbike-rental/">50cc motorbike rental</a> hub, pairs with the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">rental cost breakdown</a>, and complements the answers in the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>. The city-wide technique for carrying a passenger lives in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/riding-with-a-passenger-hanoi/">riding with a passenger guide</a>; this page keeps it specific to students on a 50cc.</p>
<nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
<ul>
<li><a href="#sec-1">Why students ride two up</a></li>
